{"duration_api_ms":80223,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d4d0b62c-faee-4f3b-b0fb-aea616484ff3","total_cost_usd":0.1488916,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11095,"cache_read_input_tokens":4538,"output_tokens":10360,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7327},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11095,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10360,"cache_read_input_tokens":4538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11095},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":10360,"cacheReadInputTokens":4538,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11095,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1488916,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":7327,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"merged_document\": \"# BIP: 39\\n\\n## Abstract\\nThis BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\\n\\nIt consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed. This seed can be later used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\\n\\n## Copyright\\nThis BIP is licensed under the BSD 2-clause license.\\n\\n## Motivation\\nA mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed. The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\\n\\nThis guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated determinism with a human-readable transcription. It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\\n\\n## Generating the mnemonic\\nThe mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits. With more entropy security is improved but the sentence length increases. We refer to the initial entropy length as ENT. The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\\n\\nFirst, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated. A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash. This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy. Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist. Finally, we convert these numbers into words and use the joined words as a mnemonic sentence.\\n\\nThe following table describes the relation between the initial entropy length (ENT), the checksum length (CS), and the length of the generated mnemonic sentence (MS) in words.\\n\\n```\\nCS = ENT / 32\\nMS = (ENT + CS) / 11\\n\\n|  ENT  | CS | ENT+CS |  MS  |\\n+-------+----+--------+------+\\n|  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\\n|  160  |  5 |   165  |  15  |\\n|  192  |  6 |   198  |  18  |\\n|  224  |  7 |   231  |  21  |\\n|  256  |  8 |   264  |  24  |\\n```\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039.mediawiki\",\n  \"decisions\": [],\n  \"dispositions\": [\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a3\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected 'letters'/'UTOXs' to 'words'/'wallets'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a4\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected 'ASCII seed' to 'binary seed'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This BIP is licensed under the BSD 2-clause license.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected license from GPL to BSD 2-clause\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a9\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected 'wallet satoshis' to 'wallet seed'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a12\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"fixed garbled spelling 'süeed' to 'seed'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b1\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"## Generating the mnemonic\",\n      \"reason\": \"fixed typo 'memonic' to 'mnemonic'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b2\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"fixed typo 'demonic' and corrected 23 to 32 bits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b5\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected units/values from '1024-2048 byts' to '128-256 bits'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected 'SHA652' to 'SHA256'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b8\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected 'start' to 'end' per BIP-39 spec\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b9\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected '12 bits' to '11 bits', consistent with table\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"mismatch\": \"\",\n  \"additions\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"a group of easy to remember letters -- for the generation of deterministic UTOXs\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 uses 'words' and generates wallets, not UTXOs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"converting it into a ASCII seed\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 seed is binary, not ASCII\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"This BIP is licensed under the BSD 2-clause license.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"This BIP falls under the GPL License.\",\n      \"basis\": \"citation\",\n      \"source\": \"BIP-39 specification, Copyright section (bitcoin/bips repository)\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39's copyright is BSD 2-clause, not GPL\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"representations of a wallet satoshis\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"the comparison is to a wallet seed, not satoshis\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"must encode entropy in a multiple of 23 bits\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 requires entropy in multiples of 32 bits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 1024-2048 byts\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 sets ENT between 128 and 256 bits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"its SHA652 hash\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"SHA652 does not exist; BIP-39 specifies SHA256\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"This checksum is appended to the start of the initial entropy.\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-39 appends the checksum to the end, not the start\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"split into groups of 12 bits\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"11-bit groups match the 2048-word index and the MS=/11 table\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":62303,"type":"result","duration_ms":80286,"uuid":"e44fd3a1-4821-428a-a3d8-926fb06f12fa","ttft_stream_ms":1190,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":1190,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
